{"object_id":"org.f2f0561f0ce2ddc5","object_type":"network","slug":"nbc-radio-network","title":"NBC Radio Network","paragraphs":["Within the Golden Radio Hour knowledge base, [[org|org.f2f0561f0ce2ddc5|NBC Radio Network]] is connected to 62 programs and 3367 program-level episode associations. The documented GRH connections span 1935-10-07 through 1973-01-27.","The most substantial program connections in GRH include [[show|the-great-gildersleeve|The Great Gildersleeve]] (486 linked recordings), [[show|fibber-mcgee-and-molly|Fibber McGee and Molly]] (467 linked recordings), [[show|dragnet|Dragnet]] (273 linked recordings), [[show|the-phil-harris-alice-faye-show|The Phil Harris-Alice Faye Show]] (212 linked recordings), [[show|the-railroad-hour|The Railroad Hour]] (195 linked recordings), [[show|x-minus-one|X Minus One]] (120 linked recordings), [[show|screen-directors-playhouse|Screen Directors Playhouse]] (102 linked recordings), [[show|the-fred-allen-show|The Fred Allen Show]] (94 linked recordings), [[show|duffys-tavern|Duffy's Tavern]] (88 linked recordings), and [[show|nbc-university-theater|NBC University Theater]] (87 linked recordings).","People most frequently credited on recordings directly associated with this network in GRH include Walter Tetley (680 linked recordings), Richard LeGrand (485 linked recordings), Arthur Q. Bryan (471 linked recordings), [[person|jim-jordan|Jim Jordan]] (470 linked recordings), [[person|marian-jordan|Marian Jordan]] (466 linked recordings), Lillian Randolph (461 linked recordings), Phil Leslie (394 linked recordings), Earle Ross (374 linked recordings), [[person|bill-thompson|Bill Thompson]] (356 linked recordings), and [[person|hal-peary|Hal Peary]] (331 linked recordings). These counts describe archive connections, not an employment claim."],"plain_text":"Within the Golden Radio Hour knowledge base, NBC Radio Network is connected to 62 programs and 3367 program-level episode associations. The documented GRH connections span